<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polemon II of Pontus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polemon II was the last client king of Pontus, a grandson of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythodoris">Pythodorida</a>. The emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> gave him the kingdom in 38 CE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> added part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> deposed him in the 60s CE and annexed Pontus to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, ending the Polemonid dynasty's rule there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polemon-ii-of-pontus.jpg" alt="Polemon II of Pontus" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polemon_II_RPC_3831.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
